WEBVTT

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.166
Let's drill the footwork for the Egyptian walk.

00:00:02.266 --> 00:00:07.033
So we're going to start.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.333
I'm going to turn my back towards you.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.900
We're going to start with our weight on the left foot.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.633
We're going to step - keep the arms out away from the body.

00:00:11.666 --> 00:00:16.833
Keep the knees bent, belly button pulled in, chest lifted shoulder blades down and back.

00:00:15.866 --> 00:00:20.733
Good, we're going to step forward on the right foot and bring the left foot to meet it here.

00:00:19.766 --> 00:00:22.300
Step and touch.

00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:23.000
Step and touch.

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:25.666
Take it back: step, touch.

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.900
Step, touch.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.900
Step, together.

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:34.000
Forward.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.900
Step, together.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.400
Keep the knees bent, belly button pulled in.

00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:40.333
Step, together.

00:00:39.366 --> 00:00:41.833
Good.

00:00:40.933 --> 00:00:43.233
Still going forward.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:46.500
And step, together.

00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:48.366
Step, together.

00:00:47.433 --> 00:00:53.233
So, try to visualize that you're walking across a pond on lily pads and you don't want to get your feet wet.

00:00:52.266 --> 00:00:56.533
So the foot's not out here, the feet are always step, and then together.

00:00:55.666 --> 00:00:59.400
Step, together, step, together.

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:01.900
As you step, don't let your ankle fall out.

00:01:00.966 --> 00:01:05.700
Keep the weight on that toe, keep that ankle pulled in nice and strong.

00:01:04.866 --> 00:01:08.333
Good.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.133
Step, together.

00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:13.666
Even if you're taking tiny steps make sure those toes come together.
